                "location": "engine/shelltest/overlay_longterm_mem_test.sh:133-140",
                "severity": "WARNING",
                "claim": "The new warning text and comments say that the next `apply` runs the longterm-mem install again. The new case calls `longtermmem_install_step` twice directly and never runs `cmd_apply`. The claim that `saw_mcp_row` triggers the step on every apply is therefore not proved by any assertion in this candidate. A regression in the apply gating would leave this test green while the message stays wrong.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  "engine/shelltest/overlay_longterm_mem_test.sh:133-140",
                  "bin/lib/longterm_mem.sh:71"
                ],
                "evidence_class": "inferential",
                "causal_disposition": "introduced"
              }
            ],
            "evidence": [
              "Every manifest path was reviewed.",
              "shellQuote returns safe paths unchanged and single-quotes all others, so installed commands for normal paths are byte-identical. The test in quoting_test.go checks this, and another test there runs each builder's command under `sh -c` with a path containing a space and an apostrophe.",
              "entryContainsBinary now matches both the bare and the quoted path, so entries written before quoting are still treated as owned and are replaced rather than duplicated. A test in quoting_test.go covers this, including a second merge that changes nothing.",
              "The `holds` rewrite compares the entry's matcher with nil or a string, so it cannot panic on odd matcher types. Its callers, the status helpers, are not shown in this candidate.",
              "Five golden merge cases are skipped by name because all families now repair owned entries that differ. This is a deliberate, documented behavior change. It does mean those cases no longer give backward-compatibility coverage."
            ]
          }
